# Case studies finder

Use a case studies finder only for projects that were actually documented, and say whether each is tested. A reader judges fit from the problem, the context and the outcome, so a result that shows only a title invites a wrong guess. For example, a lighting scene record should say which Home Assistant version it was tested on, or say that it is untested. Scope, result count, empty states, focus and the no-JavaScript fallback follow the [shared finder behaviour](../finder.html#finder-shared-contract).

## When to use it

Use it for a curated library of documented household projects or worked configuration examples.

## Home Assistant boundary

Do not label untested YAML as a proven case study. Tell a synthetic example from an installation record, and give the tested version when evidence exists.

